{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.LineRestriction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.LineRestriction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.MvPolynomial.PDeriv","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.MvPolynomial.CommRing","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Derivative","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.MvPolynomial.Funext"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_lineRestrict_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_lineRestrict_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/LineRestriction.lean#L138-L154","doc":"**A non-zero polynomial survives restriction to some line, in every direction.**\n\nNote the quantifiers: the *direction* `c` is arbitrary — only the base point has to be\nchosen.  That is because the constant term of the restriction is `P(a)`, so any `a` off the\nzero set of `P` already works, and `MvPolynomial.funext` supplies one over an infinite\nfield. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.eval_zero_lineRestrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.eval_zero_lineRestrict","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/LineRestriction.lean#L128-L136","doc":"The restriction's value at `t = 0` is the polynomial's value at the base point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.iterate_derivative_lineRestrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.iterate_derivative_lineRestrict","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/LineRestriction.lean#L116-L124","doc":"**The iterated chain rule.**  `dⁱ/dtⁱ` on the restriction is `(Dᶜ)ⁱ` upstairs — and\n`(Dᶜ)ⁱ` has order exactly `i`, which is the order bound the univariate Wronskian needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.derivative_lineRestrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.derivative_lineRestrict","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/LineRestriction.lean#L89-L114","doc":"**Chain rule for restriction to a line:** `d/dt (f(a + tc)) = (Dᶜf)(a + tc)`.\n\nMathlib has no chain rule for `aeval`, so this goes by induction on `f`; the multiplicative\nstep is the only one with content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.dirDeriv_mul_X","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.dirDeriv_mul_X","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/LineRestriction.lean#L72-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.dirDeriv_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.dirDeriv_add","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/LineRestriction.lean#L68-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.dirDeriv_C","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.dirDeriv_C","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/LineRestriction.lean#L65-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.dirDeriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.dirDeriv","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/LineRestriction.lean#L60-L63","doc":"The **directional derivative** `Dᶜ = ∑ᵢ cᵢ ∂ᵢ` — an operator of order one, which is the\nwhole reason it is worth naming. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.lineRestrict_C","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.lineRestrict_C","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/LineRestriction.lean#L56-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.lineRestrict_X","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.lineRestrict_X","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/LineRestriction.lean#L52-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.lineRestrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.lineRestrict","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/LineRestriction.lean#L45-L48","doc":"Restriction of a multivariate polynomial to the line `t ↦ a + t·c`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}